  "transcript": "Here's the spot most guys get stuck. You're in a normal conversation, you want it a little more than friendly, and you've got two bad options. Come out of nowhere and hit on her, which feels forced and contrived, or show your interest straight, which just reads as needy. Doesn't add anything new. You take what she already said, and you misunderstand it on purpose, in your favor. That's the whole move. Hearing some plain, ordinary line as a compliment aimed at you or as her making a pass at you. Language is rich. Any sentence has more in it than the literal meaning. She says, you're wearing a blue shirt. You go, woah. My eyes are up here. Stop checking me out. It came straight from what she just said, so it never feels contrived. But here's the part that actually makes it work, and the part most guys miss. You're not hitting on her. You're acting like she's hitting on you. That flip is everything. It's not about how sexual the line is. It's about who's chasing who. When you misread her, she's suddenly the one chasing you, without you showing a drop of neediness. Now the trap. Don't try to be clever with your words. Be clever with the assumption. So take what she said as the best possible thing. She wants you and then say something almost boring back. Where are we going? Somewhere innocent. Don't get any ideas. Keep it suggestive, never graphic. The best read is one she can fill in herself. Deliver it flat, like it's obviously what she meant. The straighter your face, the harder it lands. The same move also bails you out when she throws you a dig or a test. Instead of defending yourself, you decide it meant something flattering and roll with it. And this pays off well beyond dating. It's the cure for being the literal guy who takes everything at face value. Learning to hear the second meaning instead of just processing the words makes you quicker and lighter in any room. So here's the drill. A few minutes a day, any line, off the TV, out of a book, anything with I, you, or we in it. Hear it as her making a move on you, and say it back with a straight face. Keep at it, and this stops being something you reach for and becomes second nature. The read just shows up mid conversation before you've thought about it. So put in the reps. That's how you stop chasing and become the one she's chasing.",
